WEBVTT

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:05.480
<b>August 12th 2000, Groom Lake Base, Nevada</b>

00:00:13.520 --> 00:00:16.890
Drop your speed, Ghost 2! 
You're over the limit!

00:00:16.890 --> 00:00:18.410
It's too dangerous to keep doing this!

00:00:18.410 --> 00:00:20.040
Get back to the standard program!

00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:23.540
Not yet! I'm going to see 
how far I can push her!

00:00:25.490 --> 00:00:27.420
You always do this!

00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:29.100
Stop it already!

00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:32.330
Shut up! If you can't keep 
up then go back to base!

00:00:32.330 --> 00:00:33.220
What did you say?

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:36.590
We need to prove how good this 
thing is as fast as we can,

00:00:36.860 --> 00:00:39.840
or the Raptor deployment 
project will be shelved!

00:00:41.810 --> 00:00:43.230
Ghost to all units.

00:00:43.610 --> 00:00:46.250
I will take over as Ghost 2's chaser.

00:00:46.250 --> 00:00:47.640
That's nuts, Lieutenant!

00:00:47.640 --> 00:00:49.860
He's suicidal, and you're 
going to follow him?

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:52.610
Development delays are 
going to kill this TSF.

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:55.360
Somebody has to make up for it somewhere.

00:00:58.000 --> 00:00:58.940
Captain?

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:15.420
The best test pilot in Area 
51? Don't make me laugh!

00:01:15.890 --> 00:01:19.100
Your stupid pride got Lieutenant Sven killed!

00:01:22.490 --> 00:01:24.020
Say something!

00:01:24.020 --> 00:01:25.810
Say something arrogant and 
stupid like you always do!

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:30.560
Stop it! This isn't the time!

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:36.440
I'll never forgive you.

00:01:38.370 --> 00:01:41.920
You're the one who killed our captain!

00:02:12.410 --> 00:02:16.860
It must've been a lot easier to pretend to be 
a nice guy somewhere nobody knew about your past.

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:33.040
<b>The Sound of Twisted Wings</b>

00:04:08.200 --> 00:04:09.000
Hey.

00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:12.800
I heard the party last night got pretty wild.

00:04:13.980 --> 00:04:16.440
You're looking more manly than ever.

00:04:16.440 --> 00:04:18.150
Did Natalie tell you?

00:04:18.640 --> 00:04:21.330
That place is our hangout.

00:04:21.330 --> 00:04:23.680
We'll hear about it whether you like it or not.

00:04:27.240 --> 00:04:28.500
Oh my.

00:04:28.500 --> 00:04:30.410
Are we back to the Lonely Wolf?

00:04:30.410 --> 00:04:31.690
Leave him alone.

00:04:31.690 --> 00:04:34.440
Everybody wants to be left alone sometimes.

00:04:35.650 --> 00:04:39.680
That's very grown up of you to 
say, Little Miss Chobi. Have some milk.

00:04:39.680 --> 00:04:41.940
Alright, if you want a fight you've got one.

00:05:10.620 --> 00:05:17.750
These records make it clear that Rick 
Sven was killed by piloting error.

00:05:18.370 --> 00:05:23.610
Thus, the tribunal has 
determined that Ensign Yuuya Bridges

00:05:23.610 --> 00:05:27.440
was in no way at fault for the 
accident under discussion.

00:05:27.960 --> 00:05:30.010
That is all. The tribunal is ended.

00:05:33.130 --> 00:05:33.890
Yuuya!

00:05:38.420 --> 00:05:42.110
No matter what anyone says, you killed him.

00:05:42.930 --> 00:05:45.340
Don't think you can run away from that fact.

00:05:47.660 --> 00:05:50.860
If you don't want to get in 
an accident, don't follow me.

00:05:52.410 --> 00:05:53.290
You bastard!

00:05:53.290 --> 00:05:53.660
Leon!

00:06:16.100 --> 00:06:16.970
Inia?

00:06:22.300 --> 00:06:25.160
Are you guys off again today?

00:06:26.880 --> 00:06:28.920
You were crying, weren't you Yuuya?

00:06:29.810 --> 00:06:31.010
You were crying?

00:06:31.010 --> 00:06:33.530
What are you talking about?

00:06:33.920 --> 00:06:35.400
It's okay.

00:06:35.400 --> 00:06:38.290
The sad things that happened 
and the painful tears

00:06:38.760 --> 00:06:41.680
are all important memories that 
made you who you are today.

00:06:46.240 --> 00:06:46.680
Hey.

00:06:47.570 --> 00:06:49.770
Would you come with me for a bit?

00:07:09.100 --> 00:07:11.520
Ghost 2 has passed point N-3.

00:07:11.520 --> 00:07:13.860
-2.7. A new record!

00:07:16.080 --> 00:07:17.160
Not yet!

00:07:39.730 --> 00:07:40.530
Lieutenant!

00:07:42.290 --> 00:07:43.410
No!

00:07:47.650 --> 00:07:48.570
What happened to him?

00:07:49.220 --> 00:07:50.720
We have a Code 413.

00:07:50.720 --> 00:07:52.720
Ghost Team is to call off 
the test immediately.

00:07:52.720 --> 00:07:54.800
Repeat, call of the test immediately!

00:07:55.530 --> 00:07:56.460
Lieutenant!

00:07:56.460 --> 00:07:59.450
Damn it! Come in, Lieutenant!

00:08:03.820 --> 00:08:08.260
Damn it!

00:08:23.570 --> 00:08:24.600
Does it still hurt?

00:08:26.980 --> 00:08:30.360
I think Yuuya really has changed.

00:08:30.760 --> 00:08:32.680
You saw the Bao Feng fight, right?

00:08:33.400 --> 00:08:37.870
If the people around him didn't trust 
him, that duel could never have happened.

00:08:38.360 --> 00:08:42.660
They might just have been so tired 
of his selfishness they gave up.

00:08:44.960 --> 00:08:47.790
It doesn't matter how much he's changed.

00:08:48.880 --> 00:08:56.140
I'll never forgive him for running away and 
leaving the lieutenant, you, and everything else.

00:09:03.810 --> 00:09:08.180
Hey, do you know what the 
opposite of "like" is?

00:09:09.330 --> 00:09:10.940
"Hate", right?

00:09:10.940 --> 00:09:12.190
What of it?

00:09:12.890 --> 00:09:16.840
No. The opposite of 
"like" is "indifference."

00:09:18.370 --> 00:09:22.380
You're suffering from the curse you 
put on yourself too, aren't you?

00:09:34.140 --> 00:09:37.900
The accident was my fault, in the end.

00:09:38.890 --> 00:09:45.310
I had to be a good American citizen, 
and make sure everyone knew it.

00:09:46.020 --> 00:09:50.610
That was the only way to shut up the 
people who criticized my mother.

00:09:50.940 --> 00:09:52.100
That was what I thought.

00:09:53.760 --> 00:09:57.450
So I needed to rise up in the military.

00:09:57.970 --> 00:10:00.660
As fast as I could, and 
no matter what the cost.

00:10:01.980 --> 00:10:04.100
I didn't care about anyone else.

00:10:04.610 --> 00:10:06.610
The people around me were all my enemies.

00:10:08.000 --> 00:10:12.920
And it paid off, and I achieved the pinnacle 
of being an Eishi, becoming a test pilot.

00:10:13.660 --> 00:10:17.220
I was deployed to the 
elite Army TSF Research team.

00:10:25.480 --> 00:10:26.480
Why you-

00:10:37.180 --> 00:10:38.010
But...

00:10:41.410 --> 00:10:46.580
My mother died, and all I had left 
was my position in the military.

00:10:47.540 --> 00:10:49.380
That's what I started to think.

00:10:52.100 --> 00:10:54.960
And the cost of that was that accident.

00:11:01.540 --> 00:11:04.000
Sorry it's not a more interesting story.

00:11:04.420 --> 00:11:05.180
No.

00:11:05.540 --> 00:11:11.100
Maybe because we talked when we got 
stranded, I find you really easy to talk to.

00:11:11.410 --> 00:11:12.140
I see.

00:11:12.600 --> 00:11:16.980
But to be honest, I don't really 
understand what you said.

00:11:17.290 --> 00:11:18.440
I'm sure.

00:11:18.940 --> 00:11:21.860
Every time I remember it I make myself sick.

00:11:22.280 --> 00:11:23.880
No, not that.

00:11:24.730 --> 00:11:29.010
What I don't understand is why you feel 
responsible for the squad captain's death.

00:11:30.560 --> 00:11:31.730
Accidents happen.

00:11:32.180 --> 00:11:35.220
It's impossible to stop 
them from ever happening.

00:11:35.780 --> 00:11:42.130
We test pilots are risking our lives to make 
the TSFs, just like the ones on the front lines.

00:11:43.120 --> 00:11:46.410
You were the one who made the decision 
to risk your life on that mission.

00:11:46.930 --> 00:11:49.140
Your Lieutenant made the same choice.

00:11:49.580 --> 00:11:50.860
I'm the same way.

00:11:51.400 --> 00:11:53.140
I've offered my life to the USSR.

00:11:54.090 --> 00:11:56.800
Even if I lose it during a 
mission, I have no regrets.

00:11:57.210 --> 00:11:58.660
I won't blame anyone.

00:12:00.280 --> 00:12:03.690
When you blame something outside yourself 
for your own failure to do something,

00:12:03.690 --> 00:12:05.660
the only thing you can 
convince is your own heart.

00:12:05.890 --> 00:12:07.810
You can never convince anyone else.

00:12:08.340 --> 00:12:11.560
If you can't take it all, decide 
what you're going to abandon.

00:12:12.090 --> 00:12:15.530
That's what your fight is, kid.

00:12:19.010 --> 00:12:21.300
My siblings were the same way.

00:12:21.820 --> 00:12:27.550
Most of them died in the course of their 
missions, but nobody blames those who lived.

00:12:28.600 --> 00:12:30.420
You have siblings?

00:12:32.610 --> 00:12:34.040
Everyone dies eventually.

00:12:34.650 --> 00:12:39.020
It's the feelings of those left behind 
that give those deaths meaning.

00:12:40.690 --> 00:12:42.130
Cryska!

00:12:44.260 --> 00:12:46.120
Did you find something neat?

00:12:46.120 --> 00:12:46.700
Yeah.

00:12:48.000 --> 00:12:49.620
It was really pretty.

00:12:51.380 --> 00:12:54.450
It's about time for us to go.

00:12:54.720 --> 00:12:57.500
Sorry for dragging you out here.

00:12:57.740 --> 00:13:01.410
Don't worry about it. I'm 
here because I want to be.

00:13:01.410 --> 00:13:02.520
That's all.

00:13:03.680 --> 00:13:04.720
I see.

00:13:04.720 --> 00:13:05.620
You were a big help.

00:13:10.010 --> 00:13:11.820
Now let's go, Inia.

00:13:17.810 --> 00:13:20.650
Observation targets A and B are on the move.

00:13:21.010 --> 00:13:22.740
A is moving in a different direction.

00:13:24.280 --> 00:13:28.980
Continue to monitor A and B and gather data.

00:13:39.970 --> 00:13:41.790
I want to confirm something.

00:13:41.940 --> 00:13:42.990
What's this all of a sudden?

00:13:43.650 --> 00:13:45.760
You're keeping your mission and 
your feelings separate, right?

00:13:48.010 --> 00:13:49.180
What do you mean?

00:13:51.020 --> 00:13:54.300
I don't care what happened 
between you and Bridges.

00:13:54.300 --> 00:13:55.810
And it has nothing to do with me.

00:13:56.300 --> 00:13:59.140
Our job is to complete the mission perfectly.

00:13:59.840 --> 00:14:01.810
We can't fail.

00:14:02.250 --> 00:14:03.480
Don't worry.

00:14:03.480 --> 00:14:05.460
I can keep the past from 
interfering with the mission.

00:14:06.570 --> 00:14:07.740
Glad to hear it.

00:14:08.480 --> 00:14:09.160
That's right.

00:14:09.840 --> 00:14:13.740
I'm not going to be satisfied 
with being in his shadow anymore.

00:14:20.770 --> 00:14:25.180
Cheers to Argos Test Flight's victory!

00:14:25.180 --> 00:14:26.380
Cheers!

00:14:29.180 --> 00:14:30.540
What is it, Yuuya?

00:14:30.540 --> 00:14:32.420
You're never any fun.

00:14:33.460 --> 00:14:37.520
Vincent's paying today, so let's drink up!

00:14:37.740 --> 00:14:40.210
That's right. Leave it to me.

00:14:40.210 --> 00:14:42.650
I'm loaded today.

00:14:42.860 --> 00:14:47.130
Wow. What happened, Sergeant Lowell?

00:14:47.500 --> 00:14:49.780
He bet on Blue Flag.

00:14:50.000 --> 00:14:54.180
He put a ton of money on Argos 
winning their first fight.

00:14:54.460 --> 00:14:56.800
And it paid off in spades.

00:14:57.290 --> 00:15:02.670
Bao Feng was heavily favored 
to win that battle.

00:15:02.900 --> 00:15:04.760
Well, it makes sense.

00:15:04.760 --> 00:15:09.040
We've got two types of TSFs in our squad, 
and one TSF is straight off the line.

00:15:09.970 --> 00:15:12.840
And thanks to that, I made a 
fortune betting on the dark horse!

00:15:13.850 --> 00:15:17.540
I bought the mechanics drinks 
and I still had money left over.

00:15:17.540 --> 00:15:21.020
The goddess of Alaska smiled on me too.

00:15:22.310 --> 00:15:24.610
You're sure taking this easy.

00:15:24.610 --> 00:15:26.690
Did you say something?

00:15:27.290 --> 00:15:30.070
Come to think of it, Lt. Takamura is late.

00:15:34.900 --> 00:15:37.220
I'm really late.

00:15:37.220 --> 00:15:38.400
Lt. Takamura.

00:15:41.060 --> 00:15:42.090
Lt. Cui?

00:15:45.850 --> 00:15:47.050
I need to talk to you.

00:15:47.480 --> 00:15:49.180
Can I have a minute?

00:15:49.980 --> 00:15:52.840
It won't take long, if you don't make it.

00:16:00.250 --> 00:16:03.760
This is my secret technique: the beer throat!

00:16:03.760 --> 00:16:06.380
That's amazing, Vincent.

00:16:06.380 --> 00:16:08.290
That's impossible.

00:16:08.290 --> 00:16:11.150
2 seconds? A full mug in 2 seconds?

00:16:11.560 --> 00:16:13.530
He's not just smart, he's talented.

00:16:15.340 --> 00:16:17.950
Whenever he does that he's 
always out the next day.

00:16:19.330 --> 00:16:20.570
Does it matter?

00:16:20.570 --> 00:16:23.680
There's a gap in the schedule so 
there's no exercises tomorrow, right?

00:16:23.680 --> 00:16:28.210
No, that's the time when 
the mechanics are busiest.

00:16:43.660 --> 00:16:46.680
You seem even gloomier than usual today.

00:16:46.680 --> 00:16:49.090
Is it because of what happened yesterday?

00:16:50.000 --> 00:16:53.490
No. And um, I'm sorry for 
making trouble yesterday.

00:16:53.490 --> 00:16:59.450
It wasn't easy to trick the 
MPs. You owe me dinner.

00:16:59.450 --> 00:17:01.050
Yeah, got it.

00:17:01.520 --> 00:17:03.530
And this is from me.

00:17:05.400 --> 00:17:09.000
I don't think there's anybody in the world 
who doesn't have their own problems.

00:17:09.720 --> 00:17:12.000
Everybody's doing their 
best to live right now.

00:17:13.340 --> 00:17:16.440
You're from France, aren't you Natalie?

00:17:16.440 --> 00:17:20.770
That's right. But I ran 
to Canada when I was a kid.

00:17:20.770 --> 00:17:23.390
I barely remember a thing about France.

00:17:23.780 --> 00:17:26.400
I see. Sorry for asking.

00:17:26.400 --> 00:17:29.150
Don't worry about it. The past is the past.

00:17:30.090 --> 00:17:33.410
What's most important is 
that we're alive right now.

00:17:37.320 --> 00:17:40.370
But what's even more important 
is what comes next.

00:17:40.850 --> 00:17:44.010
What to do with the future is more important 
than a past you can't change.

00:17:44.010 --> 00:17:44.790
Right?

00:17:47.290 --> 00:17:48.660
You're right.

00:17:49.570 --> 00:17:51.710
And where were you born, Ensign?

00:17:52.820 --> 00:17:55.100
The middle of the countryside 
in the deep south.

00:17:56.370 --> 00:18:00.300
I figured it would be Hawaii or Los Angeles, 
there are a lot of Japanese-Americans there.

00:18:00.300 --> 00:18:05.100
No, there were no Japanese-Americans 
in the town I grew up in.

00:18:05.480 --> 00:18:07.600
It was a strict, conservative society.

00:18:08.130 --> 00:18:10.850
I see. It must've been hard.

00:18:11.380 --> 00:18:14.340
It's hard for everybody.

00:18:28.970 --> 00:18:30.930
So what did you want to talk about?

00:18:31.410 --> 00:18:32.630
What else?

00:18:33.280 --> 00:18:34.880
About Yuuya, of course.

00:18:36.130 --> 00:18:38.020
What kind of reaction is that?

00:18:38.020 --> 00:18:42.650
If you're even lying to yourself, 
then there's nothing to talk about.

00:18:42.650 --> 00:18:45.310
Lying? About what?

00:18:46.930 --> 00:18:50.010
Give up. You'll never pull it off.

00:18:52.530 --> 00:18:54.980
No, it was easier for me than most.

00:18:55.700 --> 00:19:01.600
Everybody in this base lost their country 
to the BETA, lost their families...

00:19:01.600 --> 00:19:03.330
They ran for their lives and came here.

00:19:03.700 --> 00:19:04.490
That's right.

00:19:05.220 --> 00:19:09.890
I'm sure they really want to fight on 
the front lines with their friends.

00:19:11.220 --> 00:19:12.480
It's ironic.

00:19:12.920 --> 00:19:16.020
They trained their skills so hard 
so they could defeat the BETA,

00:19:16.020 --> 00:19:17.710
so they could protect their friends,

00:19:17.710 --> 00:19:20.160
and because of that they 
were chosen as test pilots

00:19:20.160 --> 00:19:22.510
and sent to work testing 
TSFs on the rear lines.

00:19:23.060 --> 00:19:24.820
They were just like you.

00:19:24.820 --> 00:19:28.730
When they first got here they 
were all tense and miserable.

00:19:28.730 --> 00:19:29.860
I'm sure they were.

00:19:30.420 --> 00:19:31.860
But they're amazing.

00:19:32.340 --> 00:19:33.150
Amazing?

00:19:33.900 --> 00:19:38.480
They're forcing themselves to enjoy this peace 
for the sake of their friends on the front lines.

00:19:39.360 --> 00:19:41.400
They managed to change on their own.

00:19:41.690 --> 00:19:43.330
I really respect that.

00:19:43.720 --> 00:19:44.760
That's not true.

00:19:45.890 --> 00:19:53.420
The Eishi who'd come before them 
helped them change, little by little.

00:19:54.940 --> 00:19:56.920
Then they're...

00:19:56.920 --> 00:19:58.100
That's right.

00:19:58.100 --> 00:20:03.680
By doing the same for you, they're 
repaying the ones who helped them.

00:20:04.780 --> 00:20:08.250
They're passing on what they received to me...

00:20:09.810 --> 00:20:11.180
Hey there!

00:20:11.660 --> 00:20:14.650
Why are you sitting in the corner, Yuuya?

00:20:14.650 --> 00:20:16.490
Come over here and drink.

00:20:16.490 --> 00:20:18.520
Sorry, Tarisa.

00:20:18.520 --> 00:20:21.770
I was just trying to cheer 
up this lonely little guy.

00:20:22.680 --> 00:20:24.450
Who's a lonely little guy?

00:20:25.800 --> 00:20:27.130
What's that?

00:20:27.130 --> 00:20:30.840
- "Narcissist and secret pervert" is what Yuuya is.

00:20:28.900 --> 00:20:30.840
- Shut up!

00:20:30.840 --> 00:20:34.690
- "Secret pervert! Secret pervert!"

00:20:31.220 --> 00:20:34.690
- Take that back, Chobi! Take it back!

00:20:39.540 --> 00:20:41.540
Impossible?

00:20:42.130 --> 00:20:47.100
I can understand how a bird in a cage 
might long for the outside world.

00:20:47.100 --> 00:20:48.060
But it's impossible.

00:20:48.060 --> 00:20:50.720
You'll never be able to understand Yuuya.

00:20:50.720 --> 00:20:51.350
I-

00:20:52.020 --> 00:20:56.350
Can you imagine how it feels to 
be hated just for being there?

00:20:57.410 --> 00:20:58.930
Can you understand how it feels?

00:20:58.930 --> 00:21:03.360
The jealousy, the envy, the desire 
to kill someone out of hate?

00:21:03.690 --> 00:21:07.780
Have you ever tried to change someone 
in a way that makes them better for you?

00:21:09.530 --> 00:21:13.870
"I can't believe I have to entrust the 
future of the Empire to someone like you."

00:21:15.260 --> 00:21:16.710
"You're weak."

00:21:20.010 --> 00:21:25.770
The first thing you have to do in love is 
accept the other person for who they are.

00:21:26.040 --> 00:21:27.840
Did you know that, Princess?

00:21:29.560 --> 00:21:32.540
That's all I have to say. Bye.

00:21:34.400 --> 00:21:35.440
Wait!

00:21:38.080 --> 00:21:39.090
What is it?

00:21:45.360 --> 00:21:46.840
Is that all you've got?

00:22:00.480 --> 00:22:03.130
Yuuya's color really is the prettiest!

00:22:03.650 --> 00:22:05.120
Right, Cryska?

00:22:05.120 --> 00:22:07.570
That's right. Bridges is the most...

00:22:13.370 --> 00:22:14.570
I thought so.

00:22:15.570 --> 00:22:19.640
It was worth letting him go after 
he infiltrated this facility.

00:22:20.720 --> 00:22:24.200
Yuuya Bridges is the most refined catalyst.

00:22:24.200 --> 00:22:25.250
Bridges?

00:22:27.970 --> 00:22:30.910
I'll need to get another stage for him ready.

00:22:31.480 --> 00:22:33.170
Immediately.

00:24:06.570 --> 00:24:09.050
I-If it can contribute to 
humanity's coming together,

00:24:09.050 --> 00:24:10.460
I will give it serious consideration.

00:24:10.460 --> 00:24:15.530
